                <!-- §4 -->
                <h2 id="data-storage">4. How Your Data Is Stored</h2>
                <p>All user data is stored in a single JSON file named <code>flowsense_data.json</code> in the app-specific private directory on your Android device (<code>/data/data/com.flowsense.app/files/</code>). This directory:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Is <strong>sandboxed by Android</strong> — no other app can read or write this directory.</li>
                    <li>Is <strong>automatically backed up</strong> before every write operation, ensuring data integrity even if the app is interrupted mid-save.</li>
                    <li>Is <strong>protected by your device's lock screen and encryption</strong> (if you have device encryption enabled, which is on by default in Android 12+).</li>
                    <li>Is <strong>completely deleted when you uninstall FlowSense</strong> from your device, unless you have exported a backup file first.</li>
                    <li>Is <strong>not backed up to Google's cloud backup</strong> by default (we exclude the data file from Android Auto Backup to prevent unintended cloud sync).</li>
                </ul>
                <p>AI API keys you enter are stored in the same private JSON file. They are never logged, never transmitted to FlowSense infrastructure, and never included in bug reports.</p>
                <p>If you download a local AI model (Gemma), it is stored in the same private app directory. Model files can be deleted at any time via Settings → AI Engine → Delete Model.</p>

                <!-- §5 -->
                <h2 id="data-use">5. How Your Data Is Used</h2>
                <p>Data processed by FlowSense is used exclusively for the following purposes, all performed locally on your device:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Transaction display</strong> — showing your expense and income history on the dashboard, reports, and transaction list.</li>
                    <li><strong>AI categorization</strong> — sending transaction text (merchant name, amount, raw SMS/notification text) to the configured AI engine to suggest a category. With local AI modes, this never leaves your device. With Cloud AI, text goes to your chosen provider.</li>
                    <li><strong>Budget calculations</strong> — comparing total monthly spending against your configured budget limits to trigger alerts.</li>
                    <li><strong>Store Map visualization</strong> — rendering GPS coordinates of transactions on an OpenStreetMap-based map.</li>
                    <li><strong>Currency conversion</strong> — calculating amounts in different currencies using locally cached exchange rates.</li>
                    <li><strong>Report generation</strong> — computing daily, weekly, and monthly spending summaries, category breakdowns, and period comparisons.</li>
                    <li><strong>Scheduled automation</strong> — auto-adding salary and recurring expenses on configured days using Android WorkManager.</li>
                </ul>

                <!-- §6 -->
                <h2 id="no-collect">6. Data We Never Collect</h2>
                <p>FlowSense does not and will never:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Collect analytics or usage telemetry (we have no analytics SDK in the app)</li>
                    <li>Transmit your transaction history, financial data, or budgets to any FlowSense server</li>
                    <li>Create, store, or associate your data with a user account on our systems</li>
                    <li>Collect your name, email address, phone number, or any other contact information</li>
                    <li>Access, collect, or store your device contacts, calendar, or photos</li>
                    <li>Record audio beyond what Android's SpeechRecognizer processes in real time</li>
                    <li>Track you across other apps or websites</li>
                    <li>Use advertising identifiers (Android Advertising ID) for any purpose</li>
                    <li>Fingerprint your device for identification</li>
                    <li>Share your data with data brokers, advertisers, or marketing platforms</li>
                    <li>Sell your data in any form</li>
                </ul>


