                <h3>What is sent to Cloud AI providers</h3>
                <p>When Cloud AI is enabled, the following data is included in API requests to your chosen provider:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Transaction amount and currency</li>
                    <li>Merchant/description text (from manual entry, SMS, or notification)</li>
                    <li>Proposed or existing category</li>
                    <li>Contextual instructions (prompt text authored by FlowSense)</li>
                </ul>
                <div class="policy-highlight policy-highlight--warning">
                    <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M10.29 3.86L1.82 18a2 2 0 001.71 3h16.94a2 2 0 001.71-3L13.71 3.86a2 2 0 00-3.42 0z"/><line x1="12" y1="9" x2="12" y2="13"/><line x1="12" y1="17" x2="12.01" y2="17"/></svg>
                    <div><strong>Never include</strong> full account numbers, credit card numbers, government ID numbers, passwords, or PINs in transaction notes. Cloud AI requests contain only what you enter as a transaction description — keep sensitive identifiers out of that field.</div>
                </div>

                <h3>Cloud AI provider privacy policies</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Anthropic (Claude):</strong> anthropic.com/privacy</li>
                    <li><strong>Google (Gemini):</strong> policies.google.com/privacy</li>
                    <li><strong>OpenAI (ChatGPT):</strong> openai.com/policies/privacy-policy</li>
                    <li><strong>DeepSeek:</strong> deepseek.com/privacy</li>
                </ul>
                <p><strong>Important:</strong> FlowSense does not act as a proxy or intermediary for Cloud AI calls. Requests go directly from your device to the provider's API endpoint using the API key you supplied. FlowSense never sees, logs, or stores these API calls.</p>

