                <!-- §10 -->
                <h2 id="billing">10. In-App Purchases &amp; Billing</h2>
                <p>FlowSense offers a Premium subscription that unlocks advanced features. All billing is handled exclusively through <strong>Google Play Billing</strong>. FlowSense does not process, store, or have access to any payment card information.</p>
                <h3>Subscription details</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li>Available as <strong>monthly</strong> and <strong>yearly</strong> subscription plans.</li>
                    <li>New subscribers receive a <strong>3-day free trial</strong> — the subscription begins automatically at the end of the trial unless cancelled at least 24 hours before.</li>
                    <li>Subscriptions <strong>auto-renew</strong> unless cancelled at least 24 hours before the end of the current period.</li>
                    <li>To manage or cancel: open Google Play → Account → Payments &amp; subscriptions → Subscriptions → FlowSense.</li>
                </ul>
                <h3>What FlowSense receives from Google Play</h3>
                <p>FlowSense receives only a <strong>subscription status token</strong> from Google Play — indicating whether your subscription is active, expired, or in trial — along with the plan name. We receive no payment card details, billing address, or purchase price information.</p>
                <h3>Premium features</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li>Cloud AI (Claude, Gemini, ChatGPT, DeepSeek)</li>
                    <li>Application Scanner — discover &amp; connect banking apps</li>
                    <li>Budget Threshold alerts</li>
                    <li>Salary Scheduler</li>
                    <li>Scheduled Expenses</li>
                    <li>Custom Categories</li>
                </ul>

                <!-- §11 -->
                <h2 id="sharing">11. Data Sharing &amp; Disclosure</h2>
                <p>FlowSense does <strong>not sell, rent, or trade</strong> your personal information. Your financial data is not shared with third parties except in the specific, limited circumstances described below:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Cloud AI providers (user-initiated):</strong> If you configure Cloud AI mode, transaction text is sent to your chosen provider (Anthropic, Google, OpenAI, or DeepSeek) using your own API key. This sharing is entirely at your discretion and controlled by you. You can switch to local AI at any time to stop this sharing.</li>
                    <li><strong>OpenStreetMap CDN:</strong> Map tile requests include your public IP address — a standard aspect of fetching any web resource. No financial data is included.</li>
                    <li><strong>Exchange rate APIs:</strong> Rate fetch requests include your public IP and the currency code — no personal or financial data.</li>
                    <li><strong>Google Play Billing:</strong> Subscription-related interactions are handled by Google's billing infrastructure per Google's terms.</li>
                    <li><strong>Legal requirements:</strong> We may disclose information if required by applicable law, regulation, legal process, or governmental request. Since we store no personal data on our servers, any such request would yield nothing from FlowSense infrastructure — only data you hold on your own device.</li>
                </ul>
                <p>There are no other circumstances under which FlowSense shares user data.</p>

                <!-- §12 -->
                <h2 id="retention">12. Data Retention &amp; Deletion</h2>
                <p>Because all data is stored locally on your device, <strong>you are in full control of retention and deletion</strong>:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Active use:</strong> Data is retained indefinitely until you delete it or uninstall the app.</li>
                    <li><strong>Delete all data:</strong> Settings → Storage → Clear All Data. This permanently and immediately deletes your JSON data file.</li>
                    <li><strong>Delete specific transactions:</strong> Long-press any transaction → Move to Trash. Trash items can be permanently deleted from the Trash screen.</li>
                    <li><strong>Uninstall:</strong> Uninstalling FlowSense removes all app data from your device (Android standard behavior) unless you use Google's backup mechanism.</li>
                    <li><strong>Local AI model files:</strong> Settings → AI Engine → select model → Delete. Immediately frees the storage space.</li>
                </ul>
                <p>FlowSense does not retain any copy of your data on external servers, so there is no remote deletion request process. Everything you delete in the app is deleted immediately and permanently.</p>

                <!-- §13 -->
                <h2 id="security">13. Security Measures</h2>
                <p>FlowSense implements the following measures to protect your financial data:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Android sandboxing:</strong> The app's private storage directory is inaccessible to all other apps on the device (enforced by the Android OS).</li>
                    <li><strong>Device encryption:</strong> On Android 12+, device-level encryption is enabled by default. Your data file is encrypted at rest whenever your screen is locked.</li>
                    <li><strong>Automatic write backups:</strong> A backup copy of the data file is created before every write operation. This prevents data corruption if the app is interrupted during a save.</li>
                    <li><strong>Thread-safe writes:</strong> A mutex (SemaphoreSlim) ensures that concurrent write operations cannot corrupt the JSON file.</li>
                    <li><strong>No API key logging:</strong> API keys you enter are stored only in the private JSON file and are never included in log output, crash reports, or debug information.</li>
                    <li><strong>HTTPS for all network calls:</strong> All external requests (exchange rates, Cloud AI, model downloads) use HTTPS with the provider's TLS certificate validated by the Android system.</li>
                    <li><strong>No network transmission of financial data</strong> from FlowSense infrastructure — there is no FlowSense server to attack.</li>
                    <li><strong>Strict Android permission model:</strong> FlowSense targets Android 12+ (API 31), which enforces tighter restrictions on background location, exact alarms, and Bluetooth than older Android versions.</li>
                </ul>
                <p>While we implement strong protections, no security system is perfect. We encourage you to keep your device's operating system up to date and use a lock screen PIN or biometric authentication.</p>

                <!-- §14 -->
                <h2 id="rights">14. Your Privacy Rights</h2>
                <p>Because FlowSense stores all personal data locally on your device, most privacy rights are exercisable directly within the app without contacting us.</p>
                <h3>Rights and how to exercise them</h3>
                <div class="policy-table-wrap">
                    <table class="policy-table">
                        <thead>
                            <tr><th>Right</th><th>How to Exercise in FlowSense</th></tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr><td><strong>Right to Access</strong></td><td>Your full data is always visible and navigable within the app. Export a complete copy via Settings → Import &amp; Export → Export Data as JSON.</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><strong>Right to Rectification</strong></td><td>Edit any transaction by tapping it → Edit. Update any field at any time.</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><strong>Right to Erasure (Right to be Forgotten)</strong></td><td>Delete individual transactions or all data via Settings → Storage → Clear All Data. There is no remote copy to delete.</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><strong>Right to Data Portability</strong></td><td>Export your full dataset as a human-readable JSON file at any time. The format is open and self-explanatory.</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><strong>Right to Restrict Processing</strong></td><td>Disable SMS detection, notification monitoring, AI categorization, and location geo-tagging individually via Settings → Data Sources.</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><strong>Right to Object</strong></td><td>Disable any data processing feature via the relevant Settings toggle. Uninstall the app to stop all processing.</td></tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
