                <h3>GDPR (EU/EEA users)</h3>
                <p>If you are located in the European Union or European Economic Area, you have rights under the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR). Our legal basis for processing your data is <strong>legitimate interest</strong> (providing you with a functional expense tracker) and <strong>your explicit consent</strong> for optional permissions (location, SMS, camera, etc.). All processing occurs locally on your device. For Cloud AI, the legal basis is your consent — you opt in by configuring a cloud provider and entering your API key.</p>
                <h3>CCPA (California users)</h3>
                <p>If you are a California resident, you have rights under the California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA). FlowSense does not sell personal information. We do not share personal information for cross-context behavioral advertising. Since we store no personal information on our servers, CCPA access and deletion requests are fulfilled entirely through in-app controls.</p>

                <!-- §15 -->
                <h2 id="children">15. Children's Privacy</h2>
                <p>FlowSense is not directed at, designed for, or intended for use by children under the age of 13 (or the applicable age of digital consent in your jurisdiction). The app is rated for users aged 13 and older on Google Play.</p>
                <p>We do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13. Because FlowSense collects no personal information on any servers — from users of any age — there is no risk of children's data being stored in our systems.</p>
                <p>If you are a parent or guardian and believe your child under 13 has used FlowSense and stored financial data on a shared device, you can delete that data by opening the app on the device and using Settings → Storage → Clear All Data. Please also contact us (see Section 18) if you have concerns.</p>

                <!-- §16 -->
                <h2 id="regional">16. Regional Disclosures</h2>
                <h3>European Union &amp; European Economic Area</h3>
                <p>FlowSense processes personal data (location, transaction text for Cloud AI) in accordance with the GDPR. As described in Section 14, all rights are exercisable in-app. There are no cross-border data transfers to FlowSense servers because we maintain no servers. Cloud AI providers are subject to their own transfer mechanisms as described in their privacy policies.</p>
                <h3>United Kingdom</h3>
                <p>FlowSense complies with the UK GDPR as retained in UK law following Brexit. The same rights and protections described in this policy apply to UK users.</p>
                <h3>California (CCPA/CPRA)</h3>
                <p>We do not sell or share personal information as defined by the CCPA. We have no financial incentive programs tied to personal data. Your CCPA rights are described in Section 14.</p>
                <h3>Armenia</h3>
                <p>FlowSense includes dedicated support for the Armenian Dram (AMD) and rate.am for local exchange rates, acknowledging the significant use of the app in Armenia. Data handling is identical regardless of geographic location.</p>
                <h3>All other regions</h3>
                <p>We apply the same privacy-by-default principles globally. If your local law provides additional rights not described here, please contact us.</p>

                <!-- §17 -->
                <h2 id="changes">17. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
                <p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time to reflect changes in the app's features, applicable law, or our practices. We will indicate changes by updating the "effective date" at the top of this page.</p>
                <p>For <strong>material changes</strong> — such as the introduction of new data collection practices or new third-party sharing — we will provide additional notice on our website or through the Google Play Store listing description.</p>
                <p>Your continued use of FlowSense after changes are posted constitutes acceptance of the updated policy. If you do not agree with any update, you should stop using the app and delete your local data.</p>

                <!-- §18 -->
                <h2 id="contact">18. Contact Us</h2>
                <p>For privacy-related questions, requests, or concerns, please reach out through:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Feedback form:</strong> <a href="/#feedback">Leave a message on this website</a> — we respond within 30 days.</li>
                    <li><strong>Google Play:</strong> Use the "Contact developer" link on FlowSense's Play Store listing.</li>
